{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1552611-mass-production-of-magical-items","id":1552611,"title":"(Mass) Production of Magical-Items","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-07-23T09:13:41-07:00","id":1552611,"title":"(Mass) Production of Magical-Items","content":"So, in the ancient Mayan economy, there were two types of trade; subsistence-trade and prestige-trade. The later were the production of trinkets and novelties for the nobility; some were said to have magical-powers so, why not Prestige-Trade be a trade in magical-items? Now could a hedge-magician create them? I know that Mummies can produce amulets, (and the undead) and Mages from M:tA can instill tass into items; I don;'t recall reading up on a power in the book, <i>Sorcerer</i>, or in <i>Hunter's Hunted</i>. In NWoD <i>Second Sight</i>, IDK if there's a power in there that lets them do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-23T09:30:45-07:00","id":1552613,"title":"","content":"There are many ways to create magical and magical-adjacent items in both WoD and CoD. Almost every splat has the means to make something. And among themselves, trade in such items not only exists, but is relatively common. &quot;Minor&quot; splats usually have grater limitations doing it, but they are still able to make something under the right circumstances.<br /> <br /> It's just that such items aren't usually sold for money, they're too precious for that. But barter and favors are a regular occurrence in exchange for magical items, sometimes even between splats.<br /> <br /> Garou and Fera make fetishes. While those items have a religious aspect to them, they still trade among themselves (never with non-Shapechangers);<br /> <br /> Mages make fetishes, all kinds of Wonders and magically enhanced items, and they frequently trade all of those, even with Sleepers and Nightfolk. Most of those items may be used by anyone;<br /> <br /> Demons also can permanently enhance or enchant items in a number of ways, and find stuff left behind in Bastions. Nothing at all stops them from trade with whomever they want, and sometimes their goals align pretty well with giving something to someone;<br /> <br /> Changelings make Treasures and Chimera galore. The greater problem with their items is that most people would have to be Enchanted to be able to use them, but that's not out of question, and Enchanting itself can be sold as a service. And they're by far the splat with less compunction against interacting with others. While <i>some</i> secrecy is always basic care, Changelings are extremely careless. To the point of hanging out with some Vampires that effectively hurt them with their mere presence, just for fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-23T09:55:35-07:00","id":1552614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1552611-mass-production-of-magical-items?p=1552613#post1552613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's just that such items aren't usually sold for money, they're too precious for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I think this is a presentation that sometimes overlooks what money is useful for.<br /> <br /> Like, it can be nice to sell an asset in exchange for something that can be redeemed with anybody other than the person you sold the thing to.<br /> <br /> A magical subculture might not have the wealth of society at large as their money*, but I think it would still make sense for them to have some medium of exchange. It wouldn't even need to be in physical species, if everybody has accounts that can be verified.<br /> <br /> * Although again, it's nice to be able to redeem it with a greater number of people, and assuming anybody sees the faults in magically fabricating money...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-23T15:58:43-07:00","id":1552617,"title":"","content":"Mass producing and selling minor sorcery trinkets isn't as uncommon as one might at first think. You can go on Amazon right now and get power bracelets, energy crystals, charms and whatnot. Sure, best case that stuff is all fraud and does nothing, worst case it irradiates you. But there isn't really anything that would stop a WOD sorcerer from creating a bunch of minor enchanted items that actually work and sell them. Even less so in societies where magic is just an accepted part of life.<br /> <br /> The Path is called Enchantment, and on low levels it produces tools that do things a little better, or charms with weak effects. Something like a lucky charm would be relatively easy - since it can only be cast as a ritual, the more powerful the effect the longer it takes to enchant. So for mass production only weak effects are really viable.<br /> <br /> That is, unless you use M20 Sorcerer rules as written and allow additional Aspects, which would allow you to enchant <i>per area</i>. Meaning you could stack up several boxes worth of ammo and enchant them all with a single spell as long as you crafted it yourself (which is a general requirement).<br /> <br /> I would actually allow this for lesser trinkets like good-luck-charms with a weak effect, or items with slightly enhanced utility. It's not like there is a lot of money in selling those anyways.<br /> <br /> The Path is a bit tricky to handle as ST, because it can emulate effects that have their own paths (Alchemy, Warding, Healing, Fate etc.) so sometimes it's difficult to decide what it can and cannot do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-23T21:35:02-07:00","id":1552626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1552611-mass-production-of-magical-items?p=1552614#post1552614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, I think this is a presentation that sometimes overlooks what money is useful for.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>On a general sense I agree, and that's actually why I said &quot;usually&quot;, which is more generous than the &quot;almost never&quot; the books imply.<br /> <br /> I just think that in most (like, more than 50% of) cases they have two reasons not to:<br /> <br /> A) They have other services that can be traded for money, especially with rich humans, on top of other means to get what they want, so the need to sell relatively hard to make items for money is lessened;<br /> <br /> B) Usually they'll trade such items with people that can similarly provide services and items that can't be accessed in the larger market. Barter is usually the cheaper way to get access to such things.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I agree that trading for money wouldn't be as uncommon as the books say (except for werewolves, because religion), even with other supernaturals. Money is always extremely useful, as it can buy anything due to its fungibility. The real reason the game tries to make this kind of trade frowned upon is simply to keep the <b>Resources</b> Background useful, which I think it is regardless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1552611-mass-production-of-magical-items?p=1552617#post1552617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mass producing and selling minor sorcery trinkets isn't as uncommon as one might at first think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Such production isn't uncommon at all, and all modern societies accept magic as a part of life far more than most people usually admit publicly. Heck, some market places IRL had already to actively forbid fucking soul trading.<br /> <br /> But that has less to do with what society accepts from magic and more with what the splats in the game are whiling to make and sell, and to whom, given their general interest in remaining hidden (both from society and from their enemies).<br /> <br /> &quot;Mass production&quot;, to begin with, has the problem of defining what you mean by that. Most splats have serious limitation on how much they can make, and usually can't employ heavy machinery in the process. Then you get to the problem of inconspicuous distribution, how to reach buyers without risking exposure to hostile parties in any step of the process. Finally, you get to the point where you need a reason to make an actual magical item to begin with.<br /> <br /> Why sell an actual magical item to people who would just as readily accept any weird-looking trinket as &quot;magical&quot;? Splats that want to make money from the public at large don't need to produce magical items cheap, they can find ways to produce magic-looking things at scale. With their powers, they can lend extra credibility to almost any useless knicknack they <b>really</b> mass produce through mundane means, when they can't outright mass produce mundane items cheaply through their powers.<br /> <br /> No, real magical items are more probably a very niche luxury market, something that fetches the prices that better reward their rarity and the risk of the trade.<br /> <br /> <b>Garou &amp; Fera:</b> they have to use carefully made items to make Fetishes and Talens, preferably manufactured things, although they can employ Kinfolk in this step. But the main limitation is the need to get and negotiate/subdue a spirit, this isn't something that can be done in large quantities without serious repercussions (and quick depletion of locally available &quot;sources&quot;). Not to say that making such things just to make money is usually seen as a bad use of a Shapechanger's time. Talens can be made in somewhat larger quantities, but that's offset by their single use nature.<br /> <br /> For <b>Mages:</b> Fetishes still have the same limitations as Shapechangers, even without the religious factor. Wonders are hard and slow to make, on top of costly in money and Quintessence. Not to say that a Wonder creator is a reasonably specialized Mage to begin with, with relatively rare levels of <b>Prime</b> sphere. Items enhanced with <b>Matter</b> are a far more reasonable choice for something resembling mass production, although making them permanente and in large quantities would still require a powerful Mage, specially if the idea is to make them consistently.<br /> <br /> <b>Technocrats </b>are a special case, as they <i>can and do</i> mass produce Wonders. But they have two problems: for one, their production barely meets their need (actually don't meet it, not really), so they have better uses for their equipment than to sell at large quantities (and they have better ways to finance their operations, anyway). Two, they keep careful control of this equipment because releasing it to the public or other supernaturals is actually against their imperatives. Quite the opposite, they usually have self-destruct measures, retrieve teams and whatnot to make sure those items won't leave the Union. Internally they trade in those items regularly, though.<br /> <br /> <b>Demons:</b> those ones can make magical/enhanced items with ease with the right Lore, and they have few reasons not to employ this ability. If anything, most would like to keep tabs on the items they make to be sure they're furthering their plans, but doing shit for money isn't above them, and they <b>can</b> do so at large quantities, if not exactly industrial quantities. On the other hand they have a far better product in the form of Pacts, and are unlikely to focus too much on magic item production rather than on reaping Faith from prospective buyers. The items may be useful in this process, though, so they'll certainly be in the market in some quantity.<br /> <br /> <b>Changelings:</b> what actually stop them from inundating the world with Treasures and Chimeras are the Mists and Banality wracking havoc on their products. The need for the buyer to be Enchanted to even be able to perceive the items is a hard limit factor, too. The Fae usually won't mass product <i>per se</i> because that would be a quite Banal process in most (but not all) cases, and also because they usually require rare materials. But they have a well established production chain, so those limitations are far less stringent than they are on others. In fact, the Fae distinguish themselves in the sheer quantity of magical trinkets they surround themselves with: while for all the others those items are precious and coveted, a Changeling is likely to have even magical toothbrushes, plates, anything and everything.<br /> <br /> <b>Enchantment Path Sorcerers:</b> I don't know much about them, but they have to make the items themselves, isn't that true? That's quite a limitation on any form of &quot;mass production&quot;, as they can't even count on others' work. Even with an area enchantment, if that's at all possible, they'd require a lot of work to amass the amount of items to begin with. Doable, but probably not enough fot it to be anything resembling cheap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-24T03:14:25-07:00","id":1552631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1552611-mass-production-of-magical-items?p=1552626#post1552626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Mass production&quot;, to begin with, has the problem of defining what you mean by that.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. Perhaps a better term would have been bulk production. Mass production implies somewhat of an industrial scale. I meant bulk production, and think it is relatively common.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1552611-mass-production-of-magical-items?p=1552626#post1552626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Enchantment Path Sorcerers:</b> I don't know much about them, but they have to make the items themselves, isn't that true? That's quite a limitation on any form of &quot;mass production&quot;, as they can't even count on others' work. Even with an area enchantment, if that's at all possible, they'd require a lot of work to amass the amount of items to begin with. Doable, but probably not enough fot it to be anything resembling cheap.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct, the items have to be either &quot;a rare or ancient object&quot; (ie something that has an inherent affinity) or &quot;crafted by the enchanter&quot;. However, there is no detail on whether they need to be handcrafted, or how much assembly from pre-fabs counts as crafting. Do crystals or other readily available materials count as having an affinity as they do in popular culture and magical tradition?<br /> <br /> As with Mages, the actual process for enchantment depends on the Focus of the sorcerer. It can be similar to the Technocracy's situation where actual mass production is enabled through their paradigm - in fact, the Technocracy is keen on picking up these Extraordinary Citizens for exactly this reason - and the limitations are more a result of keeping the game balance than actual metaphysics.<br /> <br /> Overall, I agree with the assessment that selling fakes is more profitable for significantly less work, and true magical items would be an insider commodity sold at high prices / low quantity.<br /> The one exception I would make is cultures where customers see enchantment as an actual craft on par with pottery or basket weaving, and expect it to work beyond auto-suggestion (at least in within the WOD context). That's more of a meta-game exception though, because I like to think that an ancient Mesopotamian sorcerer peddling charms from a market stall in Ur is something that actually happened within the WOD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-24T07:02:17-07:00","id":1552633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1552611-mass-production-of-magical-items?p=1552631#post1552631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one exception I would make is cultures where customers see enchantment as an actual craft on par with pottery or basket weaving, and expect it to work beyond auto-suggestion (at least in within the WOD context). That's more of a meta-game exception though, because I like to think that an ancient Mesopotamian sorcerer peddling charms from a market stall in Ur is something that actually happened within the WOD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but how do these customers evaluate that if they aren't supernatural creatures?<br /> <br /> That's the thing. People believe in magic, and that's almost as true today as it was in ancient Mesopotamia. Artisans and sorcerers craft charms and peddle them from market stalls all over the world, including in any major US city. And many, maybe most of those people are dedicated to their craft and believe in the quality and power of their wares.<br /> <br /> What happens is that, <b>within the WoD</b>, those charms are either very minor or powerless, because their makers are common people (even if maybe with high Occult scores). And people with actual supernatural powers can fetch high prices for their products, because they're rare. And no keen eye on the part of mundane customers will change that, not to say that most people simply don't have the means to find out if something works. All splats with magic-item creation abilities also have supernatural means to detect those items and their properties.<br /> <br /> Real magic is elitist within the setting, with one exception: <b>when mundane charms actually work</b>. And that's maybe a better way to look at it.<br /> <br /> Sometimes making things that actually work is simply possible without Magic. Priests bless water every day, it only takes one with True Faith for you to have a steady supply of Holy Water somewhere. In some Reality Zones, a lot of mundane trinkets may really work because that's how reality works there. It's perfectly possible that some crafting traditions and rituals awaken the nascent spirit of the final product, just because, and spirits like that are far more common than splats.<br /> <br /> It's more likely, at least within WoD's metaphysics, that Ancient Mesopotamia (to stay with the example) had one or more of those situations applying, and so those common charms actually worked. And it may still happen in many parts of the world. In fact, it's possible that absolutely every place has some form of charm that works for real there (there are many such charms that we're so used to that we don't think about them as magical charms, it's just easier to spot it in other cultures).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-24T10:33:36-07:00","id":1552635,"title":"","content":"An additional situation that could lead to such a scenario were the ancient Earthbond Lucifer helped free (before promptly regretting it). Due to the nature of the Earthbound compared to the demons that possess human bodies in the modern nights, they had a lot more nascent power to spread around into minor items, and a lot more reason to focus on that as a way to maintain their human followers' devotion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-24T12:13:04-07:00","id":1552636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1552611-mass-production-of-magical-items?p=1552633#post1552633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What happens is that, <b>within the WoD</b>, those charms are either very minor or powerless, because their makers are common people (even if maybe with high Occult scores).<br /> [...]<br /> Real magic is elitist within the setting, with one exception: <b>when mundane charms actually work</b>. And that's maybe a better way to look at it.<br /> <br /> Sometimes making things that actually work is simply possible without Magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I see where you're coming from. My perspective is that the WOD offers Numina as an explanation why 'mundane' charms sometimes work, and the people who craft them are either latent or untrained Numina users or accidentally tapped into those powers - books often contrast Sorcery and Magick through Paradox, indicating that the former is something inherent in the metaphysics. So if the setting offers an explanation, why not use it?<br /> Ultimately the result is the same, and maybe I'm over-complicating things where there is no need for it - it's a bad habit I have.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, the Dark Ages books have some rules for folk magic which cover exactly the niche between ordinary people and Numina users, so maybe that would be the more appropriate mechanic behind those trinkets.<br /> <br /> Edit: <i>Tome of Secrets</i> has rules for Incantations (p.72ff) that allow to create low-level effects (including charms and amulets) outside of using Numina Paths and the preceding Folk Wisdom section also taps into it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 07-25-2025, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-29T13:48:20-07:00","id":1552731,"title":"","content":"I remember a piece of homebrew that I and a friend were writing before we scrapped it:<br /> <br /> The idea was a group of post-ascension war survivors of the Technocracy made a ton of silver cores, for blades, that were in theory, usable for klaives (which in their paradigm, they rationalized as relics or ritual pieces). Their plan was to take this mass of unsharpened lengths of silver, drop them off at the nearest rural Caern/Node and just say &quot;Howdy y'all! We cool?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah, there's a reason we scrapped it, but it was too funny and ridiculous to not entertain at the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28838-dafrontlinespecter","name":"DaFrontlineSpecter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-29T17:11:40-07:00","id":1552737,"title":"","content":"I mean, the Technocracy is generally aware that some mages as well as some RDs will make deals with EDEs (aka spirits) that will inhabit physical items and empower them... that it's not just ritual to Technocracy trained mages.<br /> <br /> That said... how that gesture would go over would be soooooo culture dependent. Given how easy it is to melt and reuse silver, it probably would be a more clear statement to take silver in the form of weapons that have been broken/rendered non-functional. That's a much more common sign of a desire for peace (&quot;we made these weapons to war against you, and we have broken them instead of using them.&quot;), and runs less of a risk of being misinterpreted as a flex/challenge (&quot;we have so much silver we can shower you with sword blanks and not care, bring it fuzzballs&quot;). There's a reason why there's a traditional phrase in Abrahamic parables of beating swords into plowshares to represent moving into a state of peace; rather than talking about being in a position to give your former foes ingots of steel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-29T18:26:44-07:00","id":1552741,"title":"","content":"As far as utility goes, giving the Garou fully built Klaives of enough quality to be made into Fetishes is probably a better options. Less than that, and there's no big difference between any scrap of silver you give them, it'll have to be worked anyway and silver isn't particularly hard to work with (as they already have the expertise and tools), so just give a lot of scrap silver.<br /> <br /> But giving them high-quality Klaives has the problem <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> pointed out. It's too easy to give the wrong impression, especially if this is your first presentation. Even worse if you drop them at a Caern, as the last thing any Sept want from a Mage is for the human Willworkers to know where the Caern is. Some Mage Kinfolk are even persecuted just because of that. It's a better arrangement to first have a peaceful meeting at a neutral location, and only then moving to better gifts, but never at the Caern.<br /> <br /> If you're a Mage ally to a Garou, you'll never see the Caern. Get used to it. It's not otherwise a bad idea, though. A post-war setting where the last survivors seek protection from the Garou is a very interesting proposal for a game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-30T17:14:43-07:00","id":1552756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaFrontlineSpecter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1552611-mass-production-of-magical-items?p=1552731#post1552731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember a piece of homebrew that I and a friend were writing before we scrapped it:<br /> <br /> The idea was a group of post-ascension war survivors of the Technocracy made a ton of silver cores, for blades, that were in theory, usable for klaives (which in their paradigm, they rationalized as relics or ritual pieces). Their plan was to take this mass of unsharpened lengths of silver, drop them off at the nearest rural Caern/Node and just say &quot;Howdy y'all! We cool?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah, there's a reason we scrapped it, but it was too funny and ridiculous to not entertain at the time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ever since I made that post, I couldn't get this image out of my head.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"544\" height=\"306\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.ibb.co/93r2wQtS/Apology-in-Advance.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.ibb.co/93r2wQtS/Apology-in-Advance.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.ibb.co/93r2wQtS/Apology-in-Advance.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> I don't mean to derail the thread. I just couldn't resist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28838-dafrontlinespecter","name":"DaFrontlineSpecter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-30T20:21:15-07:00","id":1552757,"title":"","content":"You'd still need a kin smith to hammer the Weaver out of those klaive blanks, embellish them, leave them hanging in the wind and/or streams of water in order to actually get Gaian spirits comfortable with inhabiting them. Just Technocratic fabrication is unlikely to be so appealing. Given the overall lack of spirit knowledge in the TU, it's not something you'd want to leave up to them. It's likely to end up cursed at best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-30T23:15:31-07:00","id":1552762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1552611-mass-production-of-magical-items?p=1552757#post1552757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'd still need a kin smith to hammer the Weaver out of those klaive blanks, embellish them, leave them hanging in the wind and/or streams of water in order to actually get Gaian spirits comfortable with inhabiting them. Just Technocratic fabrication is unlikely to be so appealing. Given the overall lack of spirit knowledge in the TU, it's not something you'd want to leave up to them. It's likely to end up cursed at best.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. Probable, but not necessary.<br /> <br /> It's possible for them to have a kinfolk among themselves, and even if not they may have enough understanding of Dimensional Science to know which kinds of EDEs should be attracted to the Klaive and which shouldn't.<br /> <br /> But that's certainly another reason for them to start with peaceful contact with the Garou, and being open to learn. Once they know what has to be done, they can still simplify/accelerate the process with <b>Dimensional Science</b>, and even without that they may simply produce cheap silver with <b>Matter</b>.<br /> <br /> How feasible it is depends a lot on which line you take as main for this game. Under WtA's cosmology it makes a lot of sense for mass produced Klaives and artificial silver to hardly if ever have the spiritual qualities needed for a Klaive. But in a Mage I'd say it's part-and-parcel of the game that anything can be done with Magic if you believe it. Surely, the Garou may be still suspicious and take some time examining the products before trying to use them, but that shouldn't be an impassable wall.<br /> <br /> The point of the thing, in this specific scenario, is for the Mages to be able to greatly improve the Garou's Fetish production in some way, and it's fair for this to be extraordinary. On an actual WtA game it shouldn't fly nearly as easy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-02T15:26:35-07:00","id":1552843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1552611-mass-production-of-magical-items?p=1552762#post1552762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not necessarily. Probable, but not necessary.<br /> <br /> It's possible for them to have a kinfolk among themselves, and even if not they may have enough understanding of Dimensional Science to know which kinds of EDEs should be attracted to the Klaive and which shouldn't.<br /> <br /> But that's certainly another reason for them to start with peaceful contact with the Garou, and being open to learn. Once they know what has to be done, they can still simplify/accelerate the process with <b>Dimensional Science</b>, and even without that they may simply produce cheap silver with <b>Matter</b>.<br /> <br /> How feasible it is depends a lot on which line you take as main for this game. Under WtA's cosmology it makes a lot of sense for mass produced Klaives and artificial silver to hardly if ever have the spiritual qualities needed for a Klaive. But in a Mage I'd say it's part-and-parcel of the game that anything can be done with Magic if you believe it. Surely, the Garou may be still suspicious and take some time examining the products before trying to use them, but that shouldn't be an impassable wall.<br /> <br /> The point of the thing, in this specific scenario, is for the Mages to be able to greatly improve the Garou's Fetish production in some way, and it's fair for this to be extraordinary. On an actual WtA game it shouldn't fly nearly as easy.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difficulty is that the Technocracy doesn't believe it, and so even developing a capacity to deal with spirits via DS doesn't let them work with getting spirits into material vessels. Being in the Technocratic paradigm means not getting the POV of Garou and most of the stuff in W:tA; even Glass Walkers are likely seen as incredibly &quot;superstitious&quot; to TU dimensional scientists, who persistently refer to spirits as EDEs and think that ancestor spirits are the echoes of some entity mimicking a formerly living being, just like with ghosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-03T03:36:12-07:00","id":1552850,"title":"","content":"The Technocracy is fully aware that EDEs can be intelligent enough to converse with, and that they can be negotiated with/forced into items to make mystic Wonders. It's not that they don't understand, it's that doing so is fairly antithetical to the Technocracy's ethos.<br /> <br /> The scenario posed that started this tangent also specified that this is a post-Union situation where the strict hierarchies aren't in place and those former agents have more incentive to get on the good side of all the critters they used to be part of keeping down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-03T22:51:45-07:00","id":1552869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1552611-mass-production-of-magical-items?p=1552843#post1552843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The difficulty is that the Technocracy doesn't believe it</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't believe in what?<br /> <br /> They definitely believe EDEs can be reflections of concepts, including nature-related concepts. If they think those reflections appear as a result of human thought instead of coming from powerful pre-human entities, does that really matters? Likewise the concept that EDEs inhabit and empower objects under certain situations, that the resonances and context affect the result, all of those are perfectly within their Paradigm.<br /> <br /> Union members would interpret those things in their own ways, and think many aspects of the Garou's POV is superstition, sure. But that just means they have alternative explanations for the same effects.<br /> <br /> More importantly, given the goal of being on the good graces of those RDs, following through their cultural beliefs is a no-brainer, believing it is irrelevant. None of the things they have to do to make those Klaives suitable has anything directly to do with their Magic. Science isn't less science if you add natural elements and whatnot to the process just as a good luck charm or a nod to a potential ally's beliefs, even if you don't believe in the effect (or, more probable, in the explanation behind the effect).<br /> <br /> Finally, a lot of the Technocratic stance on things is more the official party line than the personal beliefs of members. A lot of Technocrats are open, <i>in some degree</i>, to consider &quot;superstition&quot;, and some even fully believe it, despite never acting on those hypotheses <b>under the eyes of the Union</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-04T12:15:40-07:00","id":1552887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1552611-mass-production-of-magical-items?p=1552869#post1552869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't believe in what?<br /> <br /> They definitely believe EDEs can be reflections of concepts, including nature-related concepts. If they think those reflections appear as a result of human thought instead of coming from powerful pre-human entities, does that really matters? Likewise the concept that EDEs inhabit and empower objects under certain situations, that the resonances and context affect the result, all of those are perfectly within their Paradigm.<br /> <br /> Union members would interpret those things in their own ways, and think many aspects of the Garou's POV is superstition, sure. But that just means they have alternative explanations for the same effects.<br /> <br /> More importantly, given the goal of being on the good graces of those RDs, following through their cultural beliefs is a no-brainer, believing it is irrelevant. None of the things they have to do to make those Klaives suitable has anything directly to do with their Magic. Science isn't less science if you add natural elements and whatnot to the process just as a good luck charm or a nod to a potential ally's beliefs, even if you don't believe in the effect (or, more probable, in the explanation behind the effect).<br /> <br /> Finally, a lot of the Technocratic stance on things is more the official party line than the personal beliefs of members. A lot of Technocrats are open, <i>in some degree</i>, to consider &quot;superstition&quot;, and some even fully believe it, despite never acting on those hypotheses <b>under the eyes of the Union</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then the next hurdle is &quot;no one told us that taking all these EDEs out of the other dimension would destabilize it&quot;. Because the Garou also tried making fetishes on overtime in the Amazon, and the local Umbra did not do well with all those spirits missing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-04T13:21:58-07:00","id":1552888,"title":"","content":"The next hurdle to what?<br /> <br /> I am extremely lost as to what point you're trying to make broadly, let alone how it relates to this specific tangent.<br /> <br /> Sure, the thread is broadly about the mass production of magical items, and single Caern of Garou suddenly having enough silver to double the number of klaives in existence would overcome some potential hurdles that keeps that number low... but getting silver isn't really presented as the main bottleneck in Garou society on klaive-smithing. Given the relative factors, talen crafting (something the books usually indicate most Cliaths learn how to at least participate in) is going to be a bigger deal in ramped up manufacturing that could like to disruptions of the local Umbral ecosystem once you start making them faster than you can use them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-04T19:57:40-07:00","id":1552901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1552611-mass-production-of-magical-items?p=1552887#post1552887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then the next hurdle is &quot;no one told us that taking all these EDEs out of the other dimension would destabilize it&quot;. Because the Garou also tried making fetishes on overtime in the Amazon, and the local Umbra did not do well with all those spirits missing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, depending on a lot of factors.<br /> <br /> But that's for the characters to figure out how to deal with it in the actual game.<br /> <br /> If the Techies just offer adequate silver knives to be turned into Fetishes, then that's on the Garou, anyway. It's already a big help to have a big number of adequately prepared objects for the spirits to inhabit, but the actual Fetish creation is still on the Werewolves.<br /> <br /> The Mages themselves making the Fetishes is a possibility, but unlikely to be the first option, as it would go in the camp of &quot;too much for diplomacy&quot;. If they do start to do it, then whatever they get out of how much they do it is on them to find out, deal with and adapt.<br /> <br /> And I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>, Talens are far more likely to be a problem than Klaives. However efficient the Klaive manufacture becomes, you wouldn't need more than one per Garou in practice and getting your hands in adequately powerful spirits isn't easy anyway, so that's quite a self-contained problem. Those Technocrats don't seem to have access to an actual Autochtonia Factory, or an army of EDEs hunting Void Engineers, this is &quot;mass production&quot; only in the loosest sense. But Talens, those definitely can be mass produced in a more literal sense and become a real problem, if the people involved are stupid enough (which isn't unlikely).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}